{
 "about": "Which #text is a tag in a note body (family: twin parsers, hunter [notes] 2026-10-31). `tags` are the expected tags in order (Obsidian). The reading view (src/notes/tagShapes.family.test.ts) and the native parser (tests/note_tag_contract.rs) run these rows. `drift` marks a side that disagrees today; its test asserts the row still disagrees, so it turns red when fixed.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "label": "plain",
   "text": "a #one b",
   "tags": [
    "one"
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "in a list item",
   "text": "- #one\n- x #two",
   "tags": [
    "one",
    "two"
   ]
  },
  {
